From: pblsketch <239486537+pblsketch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 26/30] fix(layout): 이어지는 쪽 끝 조각 뒤 흐름을 그 쪽의 저장 다음 줄로 확인하고 바깥 아래 여백을 한 번만 둔다

What Hangul does: a native HWP5, non-TAC, paragraph-relative RowBreak
table with a positive offset in an empty host splits across pages. On the
page where its last fragment ends, Hangul 2024 starts the next paragraph
right after the fragment and its outer bottom margin, once. It keeps one
host line of space below the fragment only when the next paragraph's
stored line says so on that page: KTX page 26, paragraph 407 vpos 37878 =
fragment flow end + 2400 (host line 1500 + 900), the case #7642 stage 135
was written for. In issue2439_repeat_table_overlap.hwp (a repeated form),
the next paragraph's stored vpos (10560, 15840...) is not that page's
coordinate, and Hangul prints the next line 3.8px under the fragment.

What devel did:
1. c9062d96a (#7642 stage 135) adds the stored host advance
   (`stored_unconsumed_rowbreak_host_advance_hu`) after every final
   continuation fragment. Its only evidence is
   `next.vpos - host.vpos == advance`, which a folded ladder satisfies on
   any page.
2. The paint of a final continuation that has a recorded fragment
   placement moves to the placement's `occupied_bottom`, which already
   includes the outer bottom margin. It then adds the repeated fragment
   margin again (`repeat_fragment_outer_margin`).
On issue2439 page 3 these put paragraph 6 at 84.1 and paragraph 7's line
at 105.4-124.1, over its own table at 113.0. Page 4 was 19.2px low.

What changes:
- table_host_flow.rs: `continuation_successor_confirms_host_advance` holds
  when the next paragraph's first stored line equals
  `flow end + next space before + advance` in that column (1px).
- Paint (`layout_partial_table_item`) and typeset (fragment emit, through
  a separate `terminal_stored_host_advance`) apply the host advance after a
  continuation only when that check holds. Whole tables and opening
  fragments are unchanged.
- Paint marks the closing margin consumed when the placement's occupied
  bottom already covers it, so the repeated margin is not added twice.

Evidence (Hangul 2024 13.0.0.711 print through the official automation):
- issue2439_repeat_table_overlap.hwp page 3: fragment bottom 57.6,
  paragraph 6 Hangul ink 61.5 (top ~61.3); app17 61.1, devel 84.1, now
  61.1. Paragraph 7 Hangul 82.5, app17 82.4, devel 105.4, now 82.4. Its
  table stays at 113.0 (Hangul 112.5) and no longer sits under text.
- Page 4: paragraphs 9/10 Hangul 85.5/106.5; app17 85.1/106.4, devel
  104.3/125.6, now 85.1/106.4. Table 12 Hangul 193, app17 210.9, now 188.7.
- KTX (mydocs/pr/assets/issue7445/ktx-toc27/KTX.hwp) page 26 keeps the
  host line: paragraph 407 at 599.5 (Hangul about 1.5px below that ink).
- Page counts: samples/ (1423 documents) identical to devel and to 0032.
  The 50 private overlap documents render identically.
